<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumamoto Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumamoto">Kumamoto</a> Prefecture is a prefecture in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, with its capital at Kumamoto. It was formed in 1871 from the Kumamoto domain of the Hosokawa clan and covers the old province of Higo. Kumamoto Castle withstood a siege by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saigo-takamori">Saigo Takamori</a>'s rebels in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-rebellion">Satsuma Rebellion</a> of 1877, and the prefecture includes the volcanic caldera of Mount Aso.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kumamoto-prefecture.jpg" alt="Kumamoto Prefecture" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: mahlervv · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%98%BF%E8%98%87%E3%81%AE%E6%9C%9D_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
